{"index": "nt-2337", "query": "what was the most years a show lasted?", "table_markdown": "| Year | Show | Role | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1998 | Noorjahan | Noorjahan |  |\n| 2001–2002 | Kutumb | Gauri Pratham Mittal |  |\n| 2003 | Krishna Arjun | Shweta | Cameo |\n| 2003 | Naam Gum Jayegaa | Priyanka Singh |  |\n| 2003 | Kya Hadsaa Kya Haqeeqat | Mayuri / Gauri | Episode: Kab Kyun Kahan |\n| 2004–2008 | Kyunki Saas Bhi Kabhi Bahu Thi | Nandini Karan Virani | Indian Telly Award for Best Actress in a Supporting Role (2005) |\n| 2005 | Rihaae |  | Cameo |\n| 2005 | Jassi Jaisi Koi Nahin | Herself | Cameo |\n| 2005 | Special Squad | Dipika Ghosh |  |\n| 2006 | Kaisa Ye Pyar Hai | Kannan |  |\n| 2008 | Left Right Left | Capt.Shona Das |  |\n| 2009 | Kumkum – Ek Pyara Sa Bandhan | Aditi | Cameo |", "data_file": "dev_test/Distortions/Inputs/Dataset/203-csv/485.xlsx", "is_distorted": false, "distortion_type": null, "diversification_type": "original", "reasoning": "Looking at the Year column, most entries are single years, but a few span ranges: 2001–2002 (Kutumb, 2 years), 2004–2008 (Kyunki Saas Bhi Kabhi Bahu Thi, spanning 5 calendar years but lasting 4 years by subtraction: 2008 − 2004 = 4). No other range exceeds that, so the most years a show lasted is 4.", "detection_point": "none", "anomaly_evidence": "", "answer": 4, "dtype": "int"}
{"index": "nt-2218", "query": "how many causes were responsible for more than 50,000 confirmed deaths?", "table_markdown": "| Description | Total | Poland | Baltic States(Resettled in Poland during war) | Resettled in Poland during war(from USSR and Romania) | Sudetendeutsch | SE Europe\n(Hungary, Romania, Yugoslavia & Slovakia) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Total Population Before Flight & Expulsion | 16,199,086 | 11,038,826 | 145,615 | 365,622 | 3,160,216 | 1,488,807 |\n| Violent Deaths | 58,256 | 44,603 | 383 | 747 | 5,596 | 6,927 |\n| Suicides | 14,356 | 10,330 | 157 | 84 | 3,411 | 374 |\n| Deported( Forced Labor USSR) | 49,542 | 32,947 | 1,566 | 6,465 | 705 | 7,859 |\n| In Internment Camps | 80,522 | 27,847 | 952 | 1,037 | 6,615 | 44,071 |\n| During the wartime Flight | 93,283 | 86,860 | 2,394 | 738 | 629 | 2,662 |\n| In the course of the Expulsions | 63,876 | 57,814 | 3,510 | 561 | 1,481 | 510 |\n| Cause undetermined | 112,612 | 106,991 | 64 | 3,116 | 379 | 2,062 |\n| Other Misc. | 566 | - | 38 | 141 | 73 | 314 |\n| Total Confirmed Deaths | 473,013 | 367,392 | 9,064 | 12,889 | 18,889 | 64,779 |\n| Total Unsolved Cases | 1,905,991 | 1,404,993 | 19,374 | 73,794 | 287,169 | 120,661 |", "data_file": "dev_test/Distortions/Inputs/Dataset/203-csv/234.xlsx", "is_distorted": false, "distortion_type": null, "diversification_type": "original", "reasoning": "Looking at the individual cause rows (excluding Total Confirmed Deaths and Total Unsolved Cases), I need to find which have a Total value exceeding 50,000. Violent Deaths (58,256), Deported/Forced Labor USSR (49,542 — no), In Internment Camps (80,522), During the wartime Flight (93,283), In the course of the Expulsions (63,876), Cause undetermined (112,612), Suicides (14,356 — no), and Other Misc. (566 — no). That gives five causes with more than 50,000 confirmed deaths: Violent Deaths, In Internment Camps, During the wartime Flight, In the course of the Expulsions, and Cause undetermined, so the answer is 5.", "detection_point": "none", "anomaly_evidence": "", "answer": 5, "dtype": "int"}
