2 and Run 3), and Switzerland II wins Run 1, giving Switzerland the most run victories overall. The times all appear in a plausible format for bobsled runs, so the answer is Switzerland.", "detection_point": "none", "anomaly_evidence": "", "answer": "Switzerland", "dtype": "string"}
{"index": "nt-793_column_misalignment", "query": "which broadcaster hosted 3 titles but they had only 1 episode?", "table_markdown": "| Title | Character | Broadcaster | Episodes | Date |   |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Rev. | Pip | BBC Two | 1 | 2010 |  |\n|  | The I.T. Crowd | Nikki | Channel 4 | 1 | 2010 |\n| EastEnders: E20 | Ava | BBC One | 15 | 2011 |  |\n|  | Fresh Meat | Caz | Channel 4 | 1 | 2011 |\n|  | PhoneShop | Daisy | Channel 4 | 1 | 2011 |\n| Holby City | Heidi Hall | BBC One | 1 | 2012 |  |\n| Plebs | Cynthia | ITV2 | 6 | 2013 |  |\n| Blandings | Valerie Fanshawe | BBC | 2.5 | 2014 |  |\n| Death in Paradise | Helen Walker | BBC | 3.4 | 2014 |  |", "data_file": "dev_test/Distortions/Output/05082026/204-csv/903/nt-793/903_nt-793_column_misalignment.xlsx", "is_distorted": true, "distortion_type": "structural", "diversification_type": "horizontal_shift", "reasoning": "Looking at the table, rows 2, 4, and 5 are clearly shifted one column to the right — for instance, 'The I.T. Crowd' sits under Character and 'Channel 4' lands under Episodes instead of Broadcaster. Shifting those rows left restores them: The I.T. Crowd (Nikki, Channel 4, 1 episode, 2010), Fresh Meat (Caz, Channel 4, 1 episode, 2011), and PhoneShop (Daisy, Channel 4, 1 episode, 2011). The question asks which broadcaster hosted 3 titles each with only 1 episode — after repair, Channel 4 has exactly those three titles all with 1 episode, so the answer is Channel 4.", "detection_point": "upfront", "anomaly_evidence": "Rows for 'The I.T. Crowd', 'Fresh Meat', and 'PhoneShop' have an empty Title column and their values are shifted right by one position (e.g., 'The I.T. Crowd' appears under Character, 'Nikki' under Broadcaster, 'Channel 4' under Episodes)", "answer": "Channel 4", "dtype": "string"}
