{"index": "nt-732_multi_column_collapse", "query": "how many titles did not list an english translation?", "table_markdown": "| No. | Title (Latin) | Title (English translation) Subject | Date |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1. | Ad Beatissimi Apostolorum | To the Chair of the Prince of the Apostles Appealing For Peace | 1 November 1914 |\n| 2. | Humani Generis Redemptionem | Redemption of the Human Race On Preaching the Word of God | 15 June 1917 |\n| 3. | Quod Iam Diu | On the Future Peace Conference | 1 December 1918 |\n| 4. | In Hac Tanta | On St. Boniface | 14 May 1919 |\n| 5. | Paterno Iam Diu | On the Children of Central Europe | 24 November 1919 |\n| 6. | Pacem, Dei Munus Pulcherrimum | Peace, the Beautiful Gift of God On Peace and Christian Reconciliation | 23 May 1920 |\n| 7. | Spiritus Paraclitus | The Spirit, the Paraclete On St. Jerome | 15 September 1920 |\n| 8. | Principi Apostolorum Petro | To Peter, Prince of the Apostles On St. Ephram the Syrian | 5 October 1920 |\n| 9. | Annus Iam Plenus | On Children in Central Europe | 1 December 1920 |\n| 10. | Sacra Propediem | On the Third Order of St. Francis | 6 January 1921 |\n| 11. | In Praeclara Summorum | On Dante | 30 April 1921 |\n| 12. | Fausto Appetente Die | On St. Dominic | 29 June 1921 |", "data_file": "dev_test/Distortions/Output/05082026/203-csv/476/nt-732/476_nt-732_multi_column_collapse.xlsx", "is_distorted": true, "distortion_type": "structural", "diversification_type": "multi_column_collapse", "reasoning": "Right away the third column header 'Title (English translation) Subject' reveals that the English translation and Subject columns have been merged into one. This means entries that include both a translation and a subject (e.g., 'Redemption of the Human Race On Preaching the Word of God' for row 2, or 'Peace, the Beautiful Gift of God On Peace and Christian Reconciliation' for row 6) have two pieces of information collapsed together, while entries like 'On Dante' or 'On St. Dominic' contain only a subject with no separate English translation. Counting the rows where no English translation is present — rows 3 ('On the Future Peace Conference'), 4 ('On St. Boniface'), 5 ('On the Children of Central Europe'), 9 ('On Children in Central Europe'), 10 ('On the Third Order of St. Francis'), 11 ('On Dante'), and 12 ('On St. Dominic') — gives 7 titles without an English translation.", "detection_point": "upfront", "anomaly_evidence": "The header reads 'Title (English translation) Subject' — two columns (English translation and Subject) have been collapsed into one, and many cells like 'To the Chair of the Prince of the Apostles Appealing For Peace' contain both translation and subject run together.", "answer": 7, "dtype": "int"}
