{"index": "voters_1_vertical_shift", "query": "What percentage(%) of total voters are unaffiliated and active?", "table_markdown": "| Party |  | Inactive voters |  | Percentage |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Republican | Active voters | 5342 | Total voters | 0.2561 |\n| Democratic | 13916 | 7115 | 19258 | 0.3805 |\n| Unaffiliated | 21493 | 7062 | 28608 | 0.3615 |\n| Minor parties | 20118 | 40 | 27180 | 0.0019 |\n| Total | 100 | 19559 | 140 | 1 |\n|  | 55627 |  | 75186 |  |", "data_file": "dev_test/Distortions/Output/05202026_vertical_shift/voters_1_vertical_shift.xlsx", "is_distorted": true, "distortion_type": "structural", "diversification_type": "vertical_shift", "reasoning": "The table is clearly vertically shifted: the Total row shows values like 100 and 140 where large sums should be, and orphan values 55627 and 75186 appear in a dangling row beneath it. Realigning the Active voters, Inactive voters, and Total voters columns upward by one row places 20118 as Unaffiliated active voters and 75186 as the overall total voters. Computing 20118 / 75186 gives approximately 0.267576, or 26.7576%.", "detection_point": "upfront", "anomaly_evidence": "The Total row contains 100 and 140 instead of plausible sums, and orphan values 55627 and 75186 sit in an extra row below Total, indicating the numeric columns are shifted down by one row.", "answer": 26.7576, "dtype": "float"}
{"index": "nt-373_broken_rows_split", "query": "tell me the number of shows that only have one host per day.", "table_markdown": "| ET | Days available | Program | Host(s) | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 9am–10am | Monday–Friday | The Morning Click | Jamie Colby (M,T), Harris Faulkner (W–F) | Current events. |\n| 10am–10:30am | Monday–Friday |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  | Lauren Green (M), Uma Pemmaraju (T), Gregg Jarrett (W), Arthel Neville (F), Rick Folbaum (F), Heather Childers | Current events. |\n| 11am–11:30am | Monday–Friday |  |  |  |\n|  |  | FBN Live | Lauren Simonetti | Business news and information. |\n| 12pm–1pm | Monday–Friday |  |  |  |\n|  |  | On the Hunt | Jonathan Hunt | Current events. |\n| 2pm–3pm | Monday | Entertainment Hour | Ashley Dvorkin | Entertainment news, musical performances. |\n| 2pm–3pm | Tuesday |  | Kimberly Guilfoyle | Crime and legal news. |\n| 2pm–3pm | Wednesday | Defcon 3 | Kathleen Troia McFarland | Military news and information. |\n| 2pm–3pm | Thursday | Fox Car Report | Gary Gastelu | Automotive news and information. |\n| 2pm–3pm | Friday | Spirited Debate | Lauren Green | Discussion on religious topics. |", "data_file": "dev_test/Distortions/Output/05082026/204-csv/839/nt-373/839_nt-373_broken_rows_split.xlsx", "is_distorted": true, "distortion_type": "structural", "diversification_type": "broken_rows_split", "reasoning": "Right away I notice several rows are split: for example, the 10am–10:30am slot has its time and days on one row but the hosts and description on the next row, and similarly for 11am–11:30am and 12pm–1pm. After mentally merging these fragments, the full show list becomes: The Morning Click (two hosts rotating by day, not one per day), the 10am–10:30am show (multiple hosts across days, not one), FBN Live (Lauren Simonetti — one host), On the Hunt (Jonathan Hunt — one host), Entertainment Hour (Ashley Dvorkin — one host), the Tuesday 2pm show (Kimberly Guilfoyle — one host), Defcon 3 (Kathleen Troia McFarland — one host), Fox Car Report (Gary Gastelu — one host), and Spirited Debate (Lauren Green — one host). Counting shows that have exactly one host per day gives FBN Live, On the Hunt, Entertainment Hour, the Tuesday 2pm show, Defcon 3, Fox Car Report, and Spirited Debate — that's 7.", "detection_point": "upfront", "anomaly_evidence": "Rows like '10am–10:30am' and '11am–11:30am' have empty Program/Host/Description cells, followed by continuation rows with empty ET/Days columns but filled content — classic broken_rows_split.", "answer": 7, "dtype": "int"}
{"index": "horses_2", "query": "List all the jockeys for the most successful owner(s). Answer as a dictionary with owner as key and list of jockeys as value.", "table_markdown": "| Year | Winner | Jockey | Trainer |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1919 | Sir Barton | Johnny Loftus | H. Guy Bedwell |  |  |\n| 1930 | Gallant Fox | Earl Sande | Jim Fitzsimmons |  |  |\n| 1935 | Omaha | Willie Saunders | Jim Fitzsimmons | Owner | Breeder |\n| 1937 | War Admiral | Charley Kurtsinger | George H. Conway | J. K. L. Ross | J. K. L. Ross |\n| 1941 | Whirlaway | Eddie Arcaro | Ben A. Jones | Belair Stud | Belair Stud |\n| 1943 | Count Fleet | Johnny Longden | Don Cameron | Belair Stud | Belair Stud |\n| 1946 | Assault | Warren Mehrtens | Max Hirsch | Samuel D. Riddle | Samuel D. Riddle |\n| 1948 | Citation | Eddie Arcaro | Horace A. Jones | Calumet Farm | Calumet Farm |\n| 1973 | Secretariat | Ron Turcotte | Lucien Laurin | Fannie Hertz | Fannie Hertz |\n| 1977 | Seattle Slew | Jean Cruguet | William H. Turner, Jr. | King Ranch | King Ranch |\n| 1978 | Affirmed | Steve Cauthen | Laz Barrera | Calumet Farm | Calumet Farm |\n|  |  |  |  | Meadow Stable | Meadow Stud |\n|  |  |  |  | Karen L. Taylor | Ben S. Castleman |\n|  |  |  |  | Harbor View Farm | Harbor View Farm |", "data_file": "dev_test/Diversification/External_Source/workbooks/horses/disturbed/horses_structural_2.xlsx", "is_distorted": true, "distortion_type": "structural", "diversification_type": "vertical_shift", "reasoning": "The table clearly has orphan rows at the bottom — three rows with empty Year/Winner/Jockey/Trainer columns but populated Owner/Breeder columns ('Meadow Stable', 'Karen L. Taylor', 'Harbor View Farm') that have been vertically shifted down from the 1973, 1977, and 1978 rows. Sliding those Owner values up, the corrected owners are: 1973 Secretariat → Meadow Stable, 1977 Seattle Slew → Karen L. Taylor, 1978 Affirmed → Harbor View Farm; and the earlier rows already show their owners (Belair Stud for 1930/1935, Samuel D. Riddle for 1937, Calumet Farm for 1941/1948, Fannie Hertz for 1943, King Ranch for 1946). Counting appearances, Belair Stud (1930, 1935) and Calumet Farm (1941, 1948) each appear twice as the most frequent owners, so the answer is {'Belair Stud': ['Earl Sande', 'Willie Saunders'], 'Calumet Farm': ['Eddie Arcaro']} since Eddie Arcaro rode both Calumet Farm winners.", "detection_point": "upfront", "anomaly_evidence": "Three orphan rows at the bottom have blank Year/Winner/Jockey/Trainer but contain Owner/Breeder values (e.g., 'Meadow Stable', 'Karen L. Taylor', 'Harbor View Farm') that should align with rows for 1973 Secretariat, 1977 Seattle Slew, and 1978 Affirmed respectively.", "answer": "{'Belair Stud': ['Earl Sande', 'Willie Saunders'], 'Calumet Farm': ['Eddie Arcaro']}", "dtype": "dict"}
