ng": "The header row is clearly distorted — columns 3 through 7 are blank, meaning the original labels (likely Date of birth, Height, Weight, Spike, Block) were merged away. To answer the question I need the Block column, which based on typical volleyball roster structure should be column 7 (the last measurement column). Oliveira Walewska's block value is 290 cm (110 in); scanning the rest of the table, Marianne Steinbrecher (290 cm) and Valeska Menezes (290 cm) share that same value, giving 2 other players with the same block.", "detection_point": "upfront", "anomaly_evidence": "Header row has columns 3-7 blank (merged away), losing labels like Date of birth, Height, Weight, Spike, and Block", "answer": 2, "dtype": "int"}
{"index": "nt-1540_date_format_corruption", "query": "how many weeks did season 15 of comedy central presents span?", "table_markdown": "| No. in\n\nSeries | No. in\n\nSeason | Performer | Appearance | Air Date |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 268 | 1 | Tom Segura | only | 21 January 2011 |\n| 269 | 2 | Michael Kosta | only | 21 January 2011 |\n| 270 | 3 | Sheng Wang | only | 28 January 2011 |\n| 271 | 4 | Chelsea Peretti | only | 28 January 2011 |\n| 272 | 5 | Chris D'Elia | only | 4 February 2011 |\n| 273 | 6 | Nate Bargatze | only | 4 February 2011 |\n| 274 | 7 | Hari Kondabolu | only | 11 February 2011 |\n| 275 | 8 | Jack Whitehall | only | 11 February 2011 |\n| 276 | 9 | Al Jackson | only | 18 February 2011 |\n| 277 | 10 | Kyle Kinane | only | 25 February 2011 |\n| 278 | 11 | Matt Fulchiron | only | 25 February 2011 |\n| 279 | 12 | Mike Vecchione | only | 4 March 2011 |\n| 280 | 13 | Jessi Klein | only | 4 March 2011 |\n| 281 | 14 | Louis Katz | only | 11 March 2011 |\n| 282 | 15 | Jay Larson | only | 11 March 2011 |\n| 283 | 16 | Natasha Leggero | only | 25 March 2011 |", "data_file": "dev_test/Distortions/Output/05082026/203-csv/784/nt-1540/784_nt-1540_date_format_corruption.xlsx", "is_distorted": true, "distortion_type": "semantic", "diversification_type": "date_format_corruption", "reasoning": "The Air Date column appears consistently formatted as 'day Month year' throughout, so no obvious corruption affects the computation. To find the span, I identify the first air date as 21 January 2011 (episodes 268–269) and the last as 25 March 2011 (episode 283). From 21 January to 25 March 2011 is 63 days, which equals exactly 9 weeks.", "detection_point": "none", "anomaly_evidence": "", "answer": 9, "dtype": "int"}
